# NEGATIVE PIN — indirect-call `&`-param ABI, SIGIL axis cell: a BARE argument
# passed to a `&` parameter through a `Callable` LOCAL must be REJECTED at
# check time, not silently accepted and mis-lowered.
#
# This is the other half of the sigil axis: `f(&p)` (accepted, write-through —
# see callable_local_struct_amp_param_segv.gg) versus `f(p)` here. Making the
# `&` call convention correct must NOT make the bare call legal.
#
# ⚠ GREEN ON ARRIVAL (it rejected before the fix too), so it is RED-VERIFIED BY
# BREAKING THE MECHANISM (Core #12's break-and-watch):
#     break: `src/semantic/safety/helpers.rs`, the INDIRECT-path arm of the
#            ownership-mismatch check — `if false && expected != found {`
#     result: `gg check` -> rc 0, "OK: no semantic errors"  <-- the guard is gone
#     restore: `gg check` -> rc 1, `error[E_OwnershipMismatch]`
#
# The assertion deliberately matches the DIAGNOSTIC CODE, not the fixture path
# (a path substring would match the error header and green vacuously).
#
# WHY known_gaps/: zero parity-corpus inflow; the LIVE test asserts the reject.
#
# INTENDED: `gg check` FAILS with `error[E_OwnershipMismatch]`.
struct P:
    int n

void bump(P &p):
    p.n = p.n + 1

int main():
    Callable[void(P &)] f = bump
    P p = P(1)
    f(p)
    print(p.n)
    return 0
